The definition of disservice is quite clear: ill service, injury. I don't 
wish to argue that internet service is valuable to students: I believe it is.
But this is not the point. The point is whether or not a university damages or
hurts its students by not providing free internet access. Note that it is not 
sufficient to demonstrate that free internet access is beneficial, because 
this does not demonstrate the converse: that failing to provide the beneficial
thing is injurious. For example, a university does not injure students by 
failing to provide eg. free taxi rides to and from campus, even though such 
may very well be beneficial to students.

