  Unless I am completely misguided, we are talking about a system at the
University of Michigan--a state university. If this is so, the university
and the sysadmin both have a definite commitment to First Amendment protections
whether they want to or not.
 
  I look at the analogy this way. Were a good Samaritan (?) to donate a copy of
_The Anarchist's Cookbook_ to the University of Michigan library, and the
library refused to keep it on the grounds that it was "distasteful," there
might be serious legal consequences for both the library and the university.
Unless the library admins. were able to prove an extenuating circumstance for
not carrying the book (such as lack of shelf space or a clear and imminent
threat to public safety or property), there is a very good chance a court
would find their action unconstitutional.
 
