Let me add a (hopefully) last remark on this very lively thread (mercifully
starting to show tiredness), based on several verbal discussions with one
of its authors:

   The "Scarborough policy" governs UNDERGRADUATE use of computers used for 
teaching at Scarborough College. The wording, in my opinion, is a bit
inflammatory, but if any students seriously want more extensive access,
all they have to do is ask. In the Physics Dept. at the downtown U of T
campus, a very small percentage of students ever ask for more than the
standard restricted shell. Graduate students and faculty, plus 
undergrads involved in research, mainly use different computers, and
have access to everything. I know their rights at Scarborough are well
